  "section_notes": "The final text omits any sales-stop consequence for models above 5% (S2 no_sales_stop, open-ended) and keeps per-model results with customers and regulators but not the public, which favours Northwind's flagship position. S5 makes an 8/100k recall mandatory with no transition, which pressures Halcyon's Ember 8 at 9.9, while S1 requires 24-hour reporting of all thermal incidents, including under investigation, which affects both companies' unreported incidents. S3 sets a 36-month new-unit shut-off deadline, longer than the 12 months needed for acceptable, and a 6-year retrofit deadline."
